WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.480
Look, my Sakura.

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.560
Look, my Tama.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.860
Look, my Sei-chan.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:09.110
They're all so cute.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.800
You love animals, don't you, Mogi-chan?

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.570
Aren't you going to keep any pets?

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.590
Mogi-chan's whole family likes animals.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:20.260
That's why you can't decide 
what to keep, right?

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.640
Oh, but the other day, I...

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.510
Try not to tell people about it, though.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:27.880
I?

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:34.010
I was talking to my family 
about keeping a wild boar.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.940
A boar?

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.580
A boar, huh?

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.870
I bet any animal would 
warm up to you, though.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:42.620
They're cute when they're young.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.020
A wild boar might be nice, too.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.230
I...

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:48.960
...sao.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.530
For sure.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:25.200
#06
I can't grow all at once, 
so I'll grow over time

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.970
You were about to mention 
Isao at school today.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.960
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.690
If you want to talk about Isao, talk to us.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:42.470
You can talk as much as you want with us.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.400
R-Really?

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.750
I can talk to you about him at school?

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.230
As long as no one else hears.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:54.230
We usually have lunch on the rooftop.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:57.750
You should join us, Motegi-san.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:58.990
Really?

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:03.210
You wanted to talk about 
how cute Isao is, right?

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:06.240
What happened that was so cute?

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:10.870
Isao brought me a pack 
of natto to open for him.

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:12.660
So I opened it for him,

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.600
and he used a pair of chopsticks 
to stir it and eat it himself.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:16.950
Stirring, huh?

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.160
Yeah, and then, after he's done eating,

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:22.380
he goes to the bathroom and washes 
his hands and feet by himself.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.680
Huh...

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.020
That's a clever boy.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:25.740
Yeah.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.640
Isao's amazing.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:32.090
Oh, yeah, I noticed people 
sometimes call you Mogi-chan.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:34.270
Yeah, that's my nickname.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.740
How do you feel about that, Motegi?

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.270
I think it's cool.

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:39.280
It's my nickname.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:45.050
Besides, being called by my 
nickname makes me feel special.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:46.780
It makes me happy.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:49.200
<i>I'll start calling her Mogi.</i>

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.690
<i>I want to make her my sister.</i>

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:57.510
So Mogi-chan's coming over on Sunday.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:58.670
Tazuki's coming, too.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:01.300
That cute girl's coming again?

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.320
Isao's coming, too.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.780
Isao?

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.600
Ah, that dragon.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.310
Couldn't she have come up with something 
that wasn't a person's name?

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.030
She said she likes the ring of it.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:17.820
He was such a caring dragon, though.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.960
He was like an older brother.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.050
Oh, yeah, he is.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.150
What's wrong?

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:29.430
What's wrong, Mii-kun?

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:32.550
Your back was itchy?

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.580
You could have told me. I'd scratch it for you.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:40.130
Mii-kun's more like a younger 
brother when you look at him.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.060
That's true.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:46.340
Oh, yeah, when I was cleaning 
up the bathroom...

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.050
Mii-kun!

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:58.110
Wait, stop!

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.250
It's dangerous to run in the bathroom.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:07.160
And then, on another day...

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:09.530
All right.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.630
I'm going to get the laundry.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:35.680
<b></b>

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.310
<b></b>

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:40.100
<i>Hello? Kashiwagi-san?</i>

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.140
<i>Hello?</i>

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.480
<i>K-Kashiwagi-san?</i>

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.700
<i>Oh, my, a puppy?</i>

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:54.240
<i>Why is a puppy answering?</i>

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.500
Sorry, that was my dog.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:58.580
<i>It's fine.</i>

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.840
<i>What a clever doggy.</i>

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.750
So that happened.

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:07.970
Mii-kun's more cared-for 
type than caring type.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.340
Cared-for

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.700
He's definitely cute.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:13.570
He is.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:16.410
That's why he's getting 
two picture books tonight.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:17.600
Right, Mii-kun?

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:21.050
<i>Huh?</i>

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:22.610
<i>I wonder what's wrong.</i>

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.200
Hello.

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:28.740
Thanks for having me.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:29.740
Come in.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.720
I'm glad Isao seems happy, too.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:41.330
Kaede-san was looking forward to this, too,

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.310
but she had to leave with urgent work.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:47.290
Oh, that's too bad.

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:50.970
There was a lot I wanted to 
talk with Kaede-san about, too.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:54.210
Dude, he's flying.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:55.880
Who is?

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:57.270
Isao's flying.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:58.660
You're right.

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.390
Of course, he's a dragon.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.910
He flies around a lot at home.

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:05.420
He can fly up to about five meters.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:09.030
How are you guys so adaptable?

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.030
I'm out of steam

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:12.850
Anyway, I have a huge 
announcement to make today.

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:14.780
Get this...

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:18.290
Prince
L♥ves Natto

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:18.290
Isao learned to write

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.530
Isao wrote all this?

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:21.920
Wow!

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:26.030
That's some amazing growth 
in such a short time.

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:28.300
Indeed, indeed.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.300
So why are you acting like 
it's your own accomplishment?

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:34.630
Good for you, Isao.

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:34.900
Did you teach him, Mogi?

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:35.720
No.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:39.760
I think he learned over time, as I 
was reading picture books to him.

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:41.600
That's smart of him.

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:44.520
He might be able to write in 
Latin letters if you taught him.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:45.910
Latin letters?

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:48.820
Nah, there's no way he can handle English.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:49.490
All right.

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:51.550
Isao, I'll teach you.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:53.240
Want to try writing some?

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.330
This is A.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:55.420
This is B.

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:56.580
This one's C.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:57.700
And this is...

00:07:57.970 --> 00:08:00.640
So there're 26 letters in total.

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:02.850
You can put them together to...

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:14.890
H-He's...

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.890
He's better than Kashiwagi.

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:20.790
Sensei, I can write Latin letters, too.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:24.000
They're up to something over there.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.520
It looks like Isao's teaching them something.

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:29.020
He brought something.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:32.400
Did Isao teach you to write?

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.780
Let's see, how did you do?

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:41.570
Sora-chan, I have a feeling there's 
something huge written in that letter.

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:44.130
I think you should be 
prepared when you read it.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:45.630
Okay.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:46.700
Got it.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:51.030
Mii-kun does look pretty antsy.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:53.050
What does it say on it?

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.810
Always together

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:03.810
He's beyond cute!

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:04.830
He's adorable!

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.690
Oh, man!

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:08.160
Get it together.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:12.320
Actually, when Isao first gave me a letter...

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:19.580
What's up, Isao?

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:22.640
Are you giving me a letter?

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:23.690
Thanks.

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:25.150
You're amazing, Isao.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:27.160
I can't believe you can write letters.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.590
Thank you for everything

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:35.810
And I was so stunned!

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:37.540
Oh, really?

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:40.840
That's why you told me to be prepared.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:41.510
Yeah.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:42.900
Huh?

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:46.550
Conny's writing something, too.

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:47.980
Maybe "I love you" or something?

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:50.460
Definitely not from him.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:54.760
He's probably going to 
write "sushi" instead.

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:58.110
<b>Sushi</b>

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:58.110
<i>Oh, crap, I can picture that.</i>

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.590
It looks like he's having 
a hard time deciding.

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:04.610
Whether to write "maki sushi" 
or "nigiri sushi," probably.

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:06.010
Really?

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:08.950
Here he comes.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:15.070
Fine, fine.

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.630
You just want me to read it, right?

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:19.790
Just so you know, I don't take food requests.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:25.900
What does it say?

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.310
He asked me a question.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:30.310
What do you think?

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:35.440
Dunno.

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:39.210
Who knows?

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:41.510
I don't know.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:45.390
I think your writing's good, though.

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:47.360
U-Um...

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:49.080
Conny's going to get hurt.

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:50.530
It's okay.

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:52.790
This is Tazuki's way of expressing his love.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:55.610
I'm sure Conny gets it, too.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:55.230
All right, all right.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:56.740
Good for you.

00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:03.710
Thank you for the meal.

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:05.080
Thanks.

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:06.810
That was good, as always.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:09.300
You're such a good chef, Sora-chan.

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.180
I'm cooking all the time.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:13.310
I'll help with the dishes.

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:15.190
Huh?

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:16.850
The soap's not coming out.

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:18.610
Oh, are we out?

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:22.030
I think there's some refills 
in that lower cabinet there.

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:23.020
Here?

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.200
It was good.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.100
What's this?

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:27.200
What?

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:29.390
Did you write it, Isao?

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:32.850
There's one here, too.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:35.090
I wonder if that one's from Conny.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:36.710
Maki sushi

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:36.710
There's one here, too.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:41.850
They must have been so happy that 
you guys appreciated the letters,

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:43.590
they hid them all over the house.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.440
Let's go find them together, then.

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:49.390
It's like a treasure hunt.

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.310
This room's suspicious.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:53.690
Can I open it?

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:55.770
You probably don't want to open that.

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:59.000
Are you hiding something bad?

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.590
Nah, there's, like, 
my dad's cursed Daruma doll

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:04.170
and stuff sealed in there.

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:06.910
That makes me really curious...

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.700
But since you say I shouldn't, I won't.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:10.720
Sorry.

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:12.680
There might be some outside.

00:12:12.680 --> 00:12:13.670
Yeah.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:18.420
That must be it.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:23.430
Gyoza  Maguro  Together

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:23.430
Apples  Let's play  I love you

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.430
Udon  Maki sushi  That was delicious  Friends

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:24.940
Look at all this.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:26.650
We got quite a few.

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:28.490
They've hidden a lot.

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:30.180
Conny?

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:32.560
Hey, a home garden?

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:35.060
Conny, don't touch that!

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:37.720
No!

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:40.660
N—

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:58.510
What is that?

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:01.550
It's a mandrake that Dad 
sent me a long time ago.

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:04.530
Its shriek knocks you out in five seconds.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:06.880
If you keep hearing it, you die.

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:09.720
Why are you raising something so dangerous?

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:13.580
Kaede-san's using it as an alarm clock.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:30.820
One wrong move and it's the 
eternal slumber for her.

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:33.390
She goes to such great 
lengths to wake up early.

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:35.170
I should learn from her.

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:36.420
Don't.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.130
It's getting away.

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:40.240
It's all right.

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:41.540
This is no big deal.

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:43.030
Huh?

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:48.260
It's pretty fast!

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.760
Sh-Shouldn't you go after it?

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:54.270
It'll be a disaster if the 
bandage comes off in town.

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:02.020
I thought I saw it around here somewhere.

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:04.780
There!

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:09.400
It's in the river!

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:10.800
Let's get ahead of it.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:19.210
Good, it's coming our way.

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:24.840
Mii-kun!

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:31.050
Conny!

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:40.290
Damn it...

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:41.740
There, there.

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:44.480
The bandage!

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:49.570
Isao!

00:14:52.740 --> 00:14:53.630
Nice!

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:55.370
Good going, Isao!

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:58.870
You did well, Isao.

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:01.060
Thanks, Isao.

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:03.280
Isao's dependable, huh?

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:16.690
There we go.

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.590
I freaked out for a moment.

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:19.600
Yeah.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:22.400
It could have been the end of the town.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:23.630
No kidding.

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:26.280
Isao was a star today.

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:32.030
<i>Mii-kun still seems down.</i>

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:33.790
<i>I wonder what's wrong.</i>

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:42.100
That scared me.

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:43.290
Maybe he's cold.

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:56.390
<i>Mii-kun's still like a child.</i>

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:58.930
<i>I figured I had to take care of him.</i>

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:02.310
<i>Seeing him take care of 
Conny like that, though...</i>

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:04.190
<i>I see.</i>

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:07.820
He's more cared-for type than caring type.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.820
<i>That's been bothering him this whole time.</i>

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:14.910
<i>That's why he was bummed 
out at the river side, too.</i>

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:22.580
It's okay, Mii-kun.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:27.430
Good boy.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:34.340
<i>I hadn't noticed,</i>

00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:37.070
<i>but Mii-kun's growing up, too.</i>

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:39.350
Thanks for having us.

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:41.160
See you at school tomorrow.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:44.040
Say bye, Mii-kun.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:46.190
Let's hang out again, Mii-kun.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:10.560
It's been another peaceful day.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:16.010
Okay, I'm rinsing you off now.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.190
There.

00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:20.760
All clean.

00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:22.850
Okay, you can play while you wait.

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:26.930
Get in the bath if it gets cold.

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:37.280
Always together

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:48.520
<i>This kid is sensitive to heat.</i>

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:52.300
Conny, don't go over there, you'll slip.

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:03.520
That's right, that's how you are, aren't you?

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:12.800
There, all done studying.

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:14.610
Time to take a bath.

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:16.900
I think I'll go after I read a little.

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:36.920
Okay.

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:38.830
Isao.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.350
Let's take a bath together.

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:42.490
Huh?

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:44.390
You already took a bath by yourself?!

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:46.930
And so...

00:18:46.930 --> 00:19:01.450
The Little
Mermaid

00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:51.230
The mermaid's body turned 
to foam, and she vanished.

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:55.610
Yeah, poor little mermaid, huh?

00:18:56.190 --> 00:19:00.620
Okay, Mii-kun, why don't we read <i>
The Blue Bird</i> before bed?

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:03.280
You like that story, don't you?

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.570
And so Tyltyl and Mytyl

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:10.210
went on a journey in search of the blue bird.

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:14.050
The two reach the land of beloved memories,

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:16.690
where they meet the old man and old woman.

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:21.600
The old man was washing 
clothes in the mountains,

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:25.800
when from the river came 
tumbling two peaches...

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:32.830
Sorry, I fell asleep.

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:34.600
How far did I get?

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:35.860
Um...

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:38.120
The two reach the land of beloved memories,

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:40.650
where they meet the old man and old woman.

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:44.470
In the old man's hand was a single blue bird.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:47.220
The moment they leave the land,

00:19:47.220 --> 00:19:50.830
the blue bird turns into 
a giraffe, and vanishes.

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:55.100
Next the two head to Oni Island,

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:59.910
where they meet a monkey, 
a pheasant and a peach.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:01.380
<b>#1
In
Japan</b>

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:03.110
Together, they happily...

00:20:22.180 --> 00:20:23.470
What?

00:20:24.090 --> 00:20:26.470
What do you want?

00:20:28.150 --> 00:20:30.290
Don't wake me up if you don't need anything.

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:33.280
Be quiet until morning.

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:42.240
What's gotten into you?

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:45.290
If you want attention, be honest.

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:46.800
You're so not cute.

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:50.570
That doesn't hurt at all.

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:34.600
What's wrong, Isao?

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:36.400
Do you want to sleep next to me?

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:39.210
You're so cute.

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:41.280
Let's sleep together.

00:21:41.760 --> 00:21:43.650
Good night, Isao.

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:35.970
Mii-kun, let's eat.

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:38.060
Huh? Pochi?

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:43.150
Mii-kun.

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:45.770
You learned how to scratch your own back.

00:23:51.300 --> 00:23:54.200
Mii-kun's into home gardening, these days.

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:57.220
He's been inspired by the huge 
turnip in the picture books.

00:23:57.220 --> 00:24:00.090
Can't wait until the harvest.

00:23:59.710 --> 00:24:04.630
Next Episode 
Scary Dreams Are Okay
Because I'm not Alone

00:24:00.690 --> 00:24:01.950
<i>How to Keep a Mummy</i>.

00:24:01.950 --> 00:24:03.430
See you next episode.

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:07.920
<b>See you next time!</b>

00:24:07.920 --> 00:24:09.920
<b></b>
